Full texts are in LICENSES/GPL-2.0 and LICENSES/MIT.

Dual licensing is deliberate. The device trees under dts/ follow the same
convention as the arm64 Apple device trees in upstream Linux, so they can be
submitted there without relicensing, while the MIT half keeps anything shared
with m1n1 compatible with its license.

The contents of patches/ are not covered by this. They are changes to other
people's code and carry that code's license: patches named linux-* are against
Linux and are GPL-2.0, patches named m1n1-* are against m1n1 and are MIT.

Headers under include/dt-bindings/ are copies of the Linux originals and keep
the SPDX identifiers already in them.
